---- treasure.readme

Treasure chest patch for Nethack 3.4.3

The idea for this patch came from a recent post to rgrn by Kevin Wayne; I
thought it sounded fun (and fairly simple), so I implemented it.  It adds a
new chest type -- a treasure chest -- that will occasionally be generated,
filled with appropriate booty.  Of course, they are hidden in places that
aren't easily accessible...

In gameplay terms, it probably doesn't change game balance very much, but it
may provide a fun surprise for a lucky player, or a reward for a persistent
explorer.

Full description (with spoilers)

Treasure chests contain gold (somewhat more than in a typical chest sitting
around the dungeon), usually contain gems (only real gems, so no glass or
rocks), and will also sometimes contain a weapon, which is frequently a
random artifact.

Generation probabilities are low while high in the dungeon, and increase the
lower you are.  Only the main dungeon (excluding the Castle) is eligible for
treasure chests. Medusa's level is a special case: one-third of the time 
there will be a treasure chest there; on other levels the probability is much 
lower.  Typically you may expect to see one or two chests generated in the 
full dungeon.

Treasure chests may be hidden underwater in a pool or moat, or buried under
a floor, or in a STONE tile.  (How it got there is left as an exercise for
your imagination.)  If the treasure chest is hidden underwater, then
rustable items inside (right now, just the weapon) will be made thoroughly
rusty -- unless it's an artifact, in which case it is guaranteed to be
rustproof.  (After all, who would hide such a great weapon underwater if it
was going to be destroyed...)

I would expect most players to rarely discover a treasure chest.  It may make
means of detecting treasure more useful, for those who enjoy searching for
such goodies.  It provides a source for some extra gold, gives the players
some extra gems, and may help them identify glass/real gems.  It also
provides an increased chance of getting an artifact without needing to
sacrifice.  On the other hand, since an artifact is reasonably likely to go
undiscovered, it may reduce the chance of the player actually obtaining an
artifact.  This would be particularly noticable if your class-specific
artifact ends up in a chest, and therefore might not be available when
sacrificing.

Overall, it probably makes the game slightly easier.  However, I think that
the effect doesn't significantly change game balance.

Because a new object is added, I suppose that save/bones are incompatible.

One problem with the patch is that currently, nethack disallows the player
from looting anything while underwater.  That means that an amulet of
magical breathing (the topic of the original thread) isn't actually useful
for retrieving the treasure.  I thought about allowing looting underwater
only for treasure chests, though that would seem a bit inconsistent.  I also
wasn't sure doing so wouldn't break anything.  If anyone has any thoughts,
I'd appreciate it.

Other than that, it might be nice to have more variety in the places that
the chest can be hidden.  One thought I had was to put it in niches, behind
secret doors.  (Those would be much easier to find, though.)  It might also
be fun to have messages when there is a treasure chest on the level.
Suggestions are welcome.

Breakdown of files changed:
include/config.h
  Added a definition for TREASURE_CHEST_PATCH; if undefined, then the
    treasure chest stuff is not compiled.
include/extern.h
  Added function prototype for mk_artifact_nogift()
include/obj.h
  Added tresure chest to Is_box() macro
src/apply.c
  Added treasure chests to the switch in doapply()
src/artifact.c
  Added mk_artifact_nogift(), which generates an artifact for the treasure
    chest.  It differs from mk_artifact in that A_NONE indicates that
    objects of any alignment are eligible, and it does not try to generate
    the class-specific artifacts like when receiving a gift.
src/detect.c
  Added treasure chests to trap_detect()
src/lock.c
  Added treasure chests to lock_action()
src/mklev.c
  Added place_treasure_chest, which determines whether a chest should be
    placed on the current level, and handles creating and placing it.
src/mkobj.c
  Added code to create the contents of a treasure chest in mkbox_cnts().
  Slightly different locked/trapped probabilities for treasure chests and
    standard chests/boxes.
src/objects.c
  Added the treasure chest to the object list.
src/objnam.c
  Added a case for setting otmp->spe on a treasure chest in readobjnam.
src/trap.c
  Added a case for treasure chests in fire_damage.

